warn  {"category":"agent-trace","payload":{"reason":"truncated-json-stream","linePreview":"{\"summar
      y\":\"Audit result: the plan is directionally sound but is not production-ready until its
      Phase 0, versioned JSON contract exposes quarantine, capabilities, schema version, and
      independent obser"},"raw":"{\"summary\":\"Audit result: the plan is directionally sound but is
      not production-ready until its Phase 0, versioned JSON contract exposes quarantine,
      capabilities, schema version, and independent observation timestamps. The app must never parse
      human CLI output or infer that a workspace is safe to start from raw MicroSandbox lifecycle
      alone.\\n\\nExact MSW behavior: quarantine is recorded before credential mutation and remains
      even when inspection, stopping, or stopped-state proof fails. Quarantine is separate from
      lifecycle and blocks normal start, restart, exec/SSH-derived actions, push, and credential
      rebinding. Stop, status, metrics, logs, credential status, and terminal repair remain
      recovery-oriented capabilities where supported. GitHub operations are serialized with
      kernel-held locks; a verifier can retain the lock after its parent is killed. Setup
      interruption quarantines the workspace. Failed cleanup revokes host-write metadata first, then
      attempts guest-secret and Keychain removal; uncertainty fails closed. Only successful
      verification or a fully successful rollback clears quarantine. Existing quarantined
      credentials are never trusted as rollback state. The only repair path presented by the app
      must be terminal handoff to `msw github setup WORKSPACE OWNER/REPO`; never expose marker
      deletion or direct `msb` mutation.\\n\\nUX and accessibility rules: give the status item a
      stable localized label and a dynamic value such as workspace counts, highest-priority
      condition, and data age. Every workspace card must be a named accessibility group while
      preserving its controls as separate VoiceOver targets. Use headings, predictable
      dev/playgrounds/personal ordering, localized labels and help for every icon-only control,
      explicit progress values, and focus transfer to errors, confirmations, and the invoking
      control on dismissal. Announce only user-requested operation start/completion/failure and
      newly actionable critical conditions; never announce polling or continuously changing metrics.
      Charts require an accessibility chart descriptor or equivalent current/minimum/maximum/unit
      summary. Full Keyboard Access must reach and operate every command without hover, drag, or
      pointer use; provide standard shortcuts for Refresh, Settings, Quit, Escape, Return, and
      Space, with Cancel initially focused in destructive confirmations.\\n\\nReduced-motion and
      status semantics: observe Reduce Motion live and remove pulsing, rotation, animated chart
      interpolation, and spatial transitions; use static labeled progress plus elapsed time when
      enabled. Also honor increased contrast and reduced transparency. Color is never the sole
      signal: each normal, busy, stale, unavailable, quarantined, warning, and critical state needs
      localized text and a distinct glyph or shape. The menu-bar item must not distinguish amber
      from red solely by hue. CPU and memory bars always include numeric values and
      units.\\n\\nLocalization rules: place all UI, accessibility, notification, and recovery
      strings in a String Catalog; use plural variants and locale-aware number, percent, byte, date,
      and duration formatting. Do not construct sentences from fragments. Preserve workspace IDs and
      CLI commands as unlocalized left-to-right technical tokens while localizing their surrounding
      explanation. Raw CLI stderr belongs behind a localized, redacted error summary. Layout must
      support right-to-left direction, long translations, and larger accessibility text without
      truncating state or recovery actions.\\n\\nState-machine invariants: observed lifecycle,
      freshness, quarantine, credential health, and app operation phase are independent dimensions.
      Authoritative lifecycle may jump because another process can change it; optimistic operation
      text must not overwrite observation. A transport, parse, timeout, or schema error can produce
      Unknown/Unavailable or preserve a Stale snapshot, never Stopped. Quarantine dominates action
      availability regardless of lifecycle. Each field carries its own observed-at value; late
      responses are rejected by generation ID. Initial launch, wake, reconnect, and relaunch begin
      Unknown until a fresh baseline succeeds. Metrics become stale independently of status, and a
      hidden Metrics view is labeled not monitoring rather than stale. One mutation may run per
      workspace; global operations acquire affected workspaces in fixed order. A command exit is
      followed by an authoritative refresh before success is reflected. Longer-than-expected is not
      failure, and CLI timeouts must not be shortened below MSW’s readiness and cleanup
      windows.\\n\\nCrash, restart, and cancellation: persist only non-sensitive preferences and
      sanitized completed activity. On relaunch, any recorded in-flight action becomes Outcome
      unknown and is reconciled through read-only telemetry; never replay it, report success, or
      notify from it. Launch-at-login and crash recovery must never start a VM. Do not infer lock
      ownership from a lingering lock file. Closing the popover must not cancel work. Native Cancel
      is allowed only for explicitly cancel-safe telemetry, log, metrics, and tunnel processes.
      Start/stop/restart and push outcomes can become uncertain if interrupted; GitHub setup
      interruption deliberately quarantines; backup and restore require their transactional cleanup
      to finish. These operations therefore need terminal handoff or a durable helper and explicit
      CLI cancellation contract before offering Cancel. For cancel-safe children, use a uniquely
      owned process group, drain bounded stdout/stderr concurrently, signal once, wait for confirmed
      exit, and escalate with bounded grace periods; never signal an unverified reused PID.
      Cancellation and normal termination must race into exactly one terminal operation
      result.\\n\\nError and recovery patterns: show a localized cause, affected workspace, last
      successful observation, safe next action, and a disclosure containing bounded redacted stderr.
      Retry is automatic only for idempotent reads; mutation failures require refreshed state before
      retry. Missing CLI/config, incompatible JSON schema, missing Keychain credential, lock busy,
      telemetry unavailable, quarantine, permission denial, and child termination must remain
      distinct errors. A nonzero exit or signal is not proof of lifecycle state. Keep other
      workspace cards usable after a per-workspace failure. Terminal fallback commands must be exact
      argv-derived commands, never shell-interpolated user input.\\n\\nNotification policy: request
      authorization only after an explicit explanatory Settings action, request only used
      capabilities, and reflect later System Settings changes. Establish a fresh baseline after
      launch, wake, and reconnect. Notify only for deduplicated sustained unavailability, newly
      observed quarantine, unexpected lifecycle loss, or opted-in completion/failure of a long
      operation. Suppress the transition caused by the app’s own visible action, transient poll
      failures, sleep/offline periods, metrics thresholds, and initial discovery. Apply hysteresis
      and deduplicate by workspace, event, and transition generation. Notification text and deep
      links must contain no stderr, repository path, branch, commit, username, token, or credential
      metadata.\\n\\nPrivacy and redaction: the app must never read tokens, supply token environment
      variables, log process environments, persist raw command output, or place secrets in
      notifications, diagnostics, crash reports, analytics, or pasteboard. Redact at the capture
      boundary before any buffer or logger, covering GitHub token prefixes, Authorization headers,
      bearer/basic values, GH_TOKEN assignments, URL user-info/query secrets, and Keychain output.
      Use privacy-marked unified logging and bounded memory-only buffers. Arbitrary guest logs
      cannot be reliably sanitized, so treat them as sensitive, keep them memory-only by default,
      exclude them from diagnostics and notifications, and require an explicit user action to
      copy/export.\\n\\nProduction acceptance checks on macOS 26: complete all flows with VoiceOver
      and Full Keyboard Access from cold launch without a mouse; verify focus order, labels,
      announcements, chart alternatives, confirmations, and focus restoration. Toggle Reduce Motion,
      Differentiate Without Color, increased contrast, reduced transparency, dark mode, and larger
      text at runtime. Run pseudolocalized, long-string, French, and right-to-left layouts. Inject
      fresh, stale, partial, out-of-order, malformed, incompatible-schema, sleeping, and
      disconnected telemetry and confirm no false Stopped state. Exercise quarantine fixtures for
      pending setup, failed inspection, failed stop, SIGTERM interruption, failed cleanup, lock
      contention, and failed repair. Kill and relaunch the app at every operation phase and confirm
      no replay, duplicate child, false success, unsafe notification, or automatic VM start. Use
      fake executables to cover delays, hangs, signals, huge split stdout/stderr, partial JSON
      lines, and cancellation races. Seed every output sink with credential test strings and verify
      zero leakage. Verify notification denial, later permission changes, baseline suppression,
      deduplication, self-action suppression, and private payloads. Validate the signed/notarized
      LSUIElement build, launch-at-login, sleep/wake, logout/login, and repeated crash recovery.
      Repository evidence was cross-checked read-only against README.md, docs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md,
      docs/SETUP-GUIDE.md, docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md, docs/TEST-REPORT.md,
      artifacts/msw-menu-bar-app-plan.html, bin/msw, and quarantine/interruption tests. No files
      were edited and no project-wide tests, formatters, or linters were
      run.\",\"filesChanged\":[]}","redaction":{"applied":false,"ruleIds":[]},"annotations":{}}
