      self.assertNotIn(\\\"super-secret-token\\\", archive.read_bytes().decode(\\\"latin1\\\",
      errors=\\\"ignore\\\"))\\n\\n### docs detail\\nREADME.md:38:Each command asks for two
      fine-grained GitHub tokens and verifies the complete permission boundary automatically:
      read/clone from the VM, rejected guest push, successful host-only push, and cleanup. See
      [`docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md`](docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md).\\nREADME.md:88:Every process and agent inside
      one workspace can access everything in that workspace. The three workspaces are separate from
      one another and no Mac folder, Mac Docker socket, or Mac SSH agent is mounted into them. The
      guest GitHub credential is read-only and host-held; the write credential remains in macOS
      Keychain and is used only by the explicit `msw push` path.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:70:You may
      use the same verification repository for several workspaces when both token pairs include it.
      Each command performs its own end-to-end permission check.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:80:Each
      command starts a stopped VM automatically and opens a zsh login shell in
      `/workspace`.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:219:The VM can fetch and pull private repositories
      selected in its read token. Direct guest pushes are rejected by
      GitHub.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:246:msw status\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:248:msw stop
      dev\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:249:msw restart personal\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:250:msw stop
      all\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:256:msw metrics dev\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:286:The command records
      which workspaces are running, flushes and stops them, archives all VM roots and persistent
      volumes with sparse-file support, writes a SHA-256 checksum and info file, and restarts only
      the workspaces that were previously running.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:288:The archive includes
      code, Docker images, Docker volumes, databases, guest credentials, and VM state. macOS
      Keychain tokens are deliberately excluded. Treat the archive as sensitive
      anyway.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:296:Type `RESTORE` after reviewing the warning. The restore
      validates the checksum and archive paths, installs into a transaction, checks the restored
      MicroSandbox state, and rolls back automatically if health checks fail. Workspaces remain
      stopped afterward:\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:349:- The public network profile permits internet
      access but blocks direct host/private-network access.\\ndocs/SETUP-GUIDE.md:350:- A guest read
      token cannot push to GitHub, but unrestricted internet still permits source-code exfiltration
      to unrelated services.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:7:The release suite covers strict 1–65535
      tunnel-port validation, GitHub least-privilege boundaries, transactional Keychain cleanup,
      host-write metadata authorization, stale-token rejection in read-only workspaces, fail-closed
      `security(1)` deletion handling, metadata revocation before fallible credential cleanup,
      rollback safety when credential deletion fails, interruption-safe setup transactions, and
      fail-closed workspace quarantine. The exact packaged archive is also extracted into a clean
      directory and subjected to syntax, documentation, installation, GitHub-boundary, and
      deep-check smoke tests before release.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:22:- Read secret limited to the
      configured GitHub hosts.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:36:- Start, stop, restart, resize,
      missing-token guard, and SSH proxy behavior.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:41:- Complete GitHub setup
      transaction: read token binding, guest push rejection, host push success, temporary-branch
      cleanup, token secrecy, status, and removal.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:42:- Identical read/write
      token rejection.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:43:- Failed verification restoring the previous working
      tokens and metadata.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:44:- Detection and rollback when the guest token
      has write permission.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:49:- Detached HEAD, non-GitHub origin, missing
      host token, and user-cancel failure paths.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:56:- Read-only setup retains
      guest read access without a host token and blocks stale write-token pushes using workspace
      metadata.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:57:- Read-only conversion revokes existing host-write metadata
      before downgrade cleanup; failure leaves subsequent pushes blocked.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:58:-
      Keychain deletion rejects delete failures, post-delete lookup failures, and still-present
      items while accepting explicit missing-item results.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:59:- Remove revokes
      host-write metadata before credential cleanup; a failed Keychain delete leaves subsequent
      pushes blocked.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:60:- Failed setup rollback revokes active metadata
      before credential cleanup; deletion failures leave subsequent pushes
      blocked.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:61:- Failed guest-secret removal stops and quarantines the
      workspace so normal starts, restarts, pushes, and guest commands cannot rebind or use the
      secret.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:62:- Proven-stop quarantine handling is fail-closed when ping or
      inspect is unavailable, or stop fails.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:63:- Per-workspace GitHub
      setup/remove locks serialize credential, metadata, and quarantine
      mutations.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:64:- Dead-owner recovery migrates legacy lock directories and
      uses kernel-held `lockf` ownership, so stale or empty lock files do not wedge future
      operations.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:65:- Standalone verification blocks removal through
      `SIGKILL`, and an orphaned setup verifier retains the lock after its parent
      dies.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:66:- An interrupted verification followed by a failed repair never
      restores tainted credentials or metadata and leaves the quarantine marker in
      place.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:71:- Cold backup restoring only the previously running VM set and
      excluding Keychain credentials.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:76:- Interrupted/failing compression
      restarting prior VMs and leaving no partial archive.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:86:- The real guest
      read token is absent from simulated VM state; only the MicroSandbox placeholder is visible in
      the guest.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:87:- The write token is retrieved only by the host askpass
      helper from macOS Keychain.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:88:- The privileged push process uses an
      empty environment, temporary home, no system/global Git config, no custom hooks, no SSH agent,
      and no ambient GitHub token.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:90:- Remove revokes host-write metadata
      before secret and Keychain cleanup, so cleanup failures cannot leave pushes
      authorized.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:91:- Failed setup rollback restores old metadata only after
      all credential operations succeed; any rollback failure leaves the metadata gate
      absent.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:92:- Failed rollback secret cleanup stops and quarantines the
      workspace; normal start, restart, and exec paths refuse the quarantined
      workspace.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:93:- Setup writes and retains a quarantine marker before
      credential mutation, and clears it only after verification or a fully successful
      rollback.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:96:- GitHub setup and restore are transactional and roll back
      on failure.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:97:- Keychain deletion accepts only an explicit missing-item
      result or confirmed removal; other failures abort the transaction.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:99:-
      Backups exclude macOS Keychain tokens and remove partial output on
      failure.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:105:The portable simulator suite cannot instantiate Apple's
      Virtualization framework, alter macOS loopback/LaunchDaemon state, access macOS Keychain, open
      Ghostty/Zed, or contact GitHub with real credentials. It validates the packaged shell/Python
      behavior, state transitions, local Git flows, and security boundaries using simulated
      MicroSandbox state, a fake `security(1)` command, and local
      remotes.\\ndocs/TEST-REPORT.md:109:A real Apple Silicon macOS run against MicroSandbox v0.6.8
      independently passed VM startup, systemd, Docker/containerd, SSH, GitHub connectivity, and
      published-port checks. The full host setup did not complete workspace recreation: it reached
      browser/loopback configuration and then stopped because `sudo` requires an interactive
      terminal and password. Rerun `./setup.sh --recreate-workspaces` from an interactive
      terminal.\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:48:msw github status
      [WORKSPACE|all]\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:149:msw stop
      [WORKSPACE|all]\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:150:msw restart
      [WORKSPACE|all]\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:151:msw status\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:159:msw stop
      playgrounds\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:160:msw restart dev\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:161:msw
      status\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:165:Entering with Ghostty, opening in Zed, or using `msw open`
      starts a stopped VM automatically.\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:170:msw metrics
      [WORKSPACE|all]\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:183:msw metrics dev\\ndocs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md:206:A
      backup automatically stops and restarts only the VMs that were running. Restore leaves all VMs
      stopped.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:3:This setup uses two different fine-grained personal access
      tokens for each workspace:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:5:1. A **guest read token**. It lets the VM
      clone, fetch, and pull selected private repositories. GitHub rejects pushes made with
      it.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:6:2. A **host write token**. It stays in macOS Keychain and is used
      only when you explicitly run `msw push` or the permission
      verifier.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:16:The command stores only the guest read token and removes
      any host write token for that workspace.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:18:## Before creating
      tokens\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:23:- Be selected in both tokens.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:24:-
      Permit the host token to create and delete a temporary
      branch.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:29:Fine-grained tokens are scoped to one resource owner. A
      workspace that needs private repositories from two different owners normally needs to be split
      by owner, or one set of repositories must use another authentication mechanism. Public
      repositories do not require the private read token.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:31:## Token 1:
      guest read-only token\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:33:In GitHub, create a new **fine-grained
      personal access token** with:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:52:An organization may require an
      administrator to approve the token before private-repository access
      works.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:54:## Token 2: host write token\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:56:Create
      a second fine-grained token:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:61:Resource owner: same owner as the read
      token\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:80:No administration, secrets, webhooks, organization, or other
      write permissions are required by MSW.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:82:The host token's selected
      repository list is the definitive set of repositories `msw push` can
      modify.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:92:Paste the guest read token, then the host write token. Input
      is hidden.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:100:This prompts for only the guest token. `msw github
      verify playgrounds` reruns the read-only check.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:104:1. Stores both
      tokens in macOS Keychain under separate services.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:105:2. Binds only the
      read token to the VM through MicroSandbox secret
      substitution.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:124:Using different selected-repository lists for each
      pair provides meaningful separation. You may use tokens from the same GitHub
      account.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:130:Show only credential presence and the recorded
      verification repository; tokens are never printed:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:133:msw github
      status all\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:142:Rotate either token by running setup
      again:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:148:Remove both credentials and the guest secret
      binding:\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:154:Setup, verification, and removal are serialized per
      workspace. Setup's verifier retains the inherited lock if its parent exits unexpectedly. The
      lock file may remain after a command, but its kernel-held `lockf` ownership is released
      automatically on exit or crash, so stale files do not block later
      operations.\\ndocs/GITHUB-SETUP.md:172:The guest sees a MicroSandbox placeholder, not the real
