info  {"category":"agent-session","raw":"{\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-07T13:51:44.339Z\",\"type\":\"resp
      onse_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"custom_tool_call_output\",\"call_id\":\"call_cCQWnjNvKJRrR
      qvk1135gJYa\",\"output\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"Script completed\\nWall time 0.1
      seconds\\nOutput:\\n\"},{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"Warning: truncated output
      (original token count: 11202)\\nTotal output lines: 891\\n\\n### plan contract\\n <h3>Command
      adapter contract</h3>\\n <div class=\\\"callout success\\\"><strong>Current safe
      path:</strong> invoke <code>msw</code> for all policy-bearing mutations and terminal handoffs.
      For read-only telemetry, use <code>msb status --all --label msw.managed=true --format
      json</code>, <code>msb inspect NAME --format json</code>, <code>msb metrics --all --format
      json</code> or <code>--follow</code>, and <code>msw logs NAME --json --follow</code>. Do not
      parse <code>msw status</code> tables or <code>msw metrics --watch</code> terminal
      output.</div>\\n <p>Add a small versioned machine-readable surface to <code>msw</code> before
      production UI work:</p>\\n <ul>\\n <li><code>msw status --format json</code>: schema version,
      MSW/MSB versions, workspace IDs, lifecycle state, resource configuration, hostnames/IPs,
      published ports, GitHub credential presence/access mode, verification metadata, quarantine
      state, capabilities, and timestamp. Never include token values.</li>\\n <li><code>msw metrics
      [TARGET] --format json --once</code> and <code>--follow</code>: preserve the existing human
      default while exposing a stable JSON contract.</li>\\n <li><code>msw github status --format
      json</code>, <code>msw repos WORKSPACE --format json</code>, and <code>msw ports [TARGET]
      --format json</code>.</li>\\n <li>Later: structured preview/result modes for
      <code>push</code>, <code>backup</code>, <code>restore</code>, and <code>disk</code>. Until
      then, keep those workflows terminal-visible.</li>\\n </ul>\\n <p class=\\\"small\\\">This
      avoids sourcing or parsing <code>config.sh</code> in Swift and avoids coupling the app to
      MicroSandbox’s incidental JSON fields. Human CLI output remains unchanged.</p>\\n\\n
      <h3>Suggested domain types</h3>\\n <pre>WorkspaceID = dev | playgrounds | personal\\nLifecycle
      = running | stopped | starting | stopping | restarting | missing | unavailable\\nFreshness =
      current(observedAt) | stale(lastObservedAt) | unknown\\nWorkspaceSnapshot = {\\n id, purpose,
      host, ip, lifecycle, resources, metrics?, github?, quarantine?, freshness\\n}\\nOperation = {
      id, workspace?, kind, phase, startedAt, outputTail, result }\\nMetricsSnapshot = { cpuPercent,
      memoryUsed, memoryLimit, network, diskIO, uptime, observedAt }</pre>\\n\\n <h2>5. Polling,
      freshness, and notifications</h2>\\n <div class=\\\"grid\\\">\\n <section
      class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Status cadence</h3><p>Read status immediately on launch and when the
      popover opens. Poll every 10–15 seconds while the app is active. Background polling must never
      call a command that starts a VM.</p></section>\\n <section class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Metrics
      cadence</h3><p>Show compact metrics from the latest snapshot. Stream or poll every 2–5 seconds
      only while the detail Metrics view is visible; stop the stream when it
      closes.</p></section>\\n <section class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Stale data</h3><p>Every field has an
      observed-at timestamp. On failure, preserve the last good value with a visible Stale badge and
      Retry. Never convert a transport error into “Stopped”.</p></section>\\n <section
      class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Notifications</h3><p>Request notification permission only from an
      explicit Settings toggle. Notify only after an initial baseline and only for deduplicated
      meaningful transitions or failed long-running operations. Suppress alerts caused by the app’s
      own action.</p></section>\\n </div>\\n\\n <h2>6. Safety and UX guardrails</h2>\\n <div
      class=\\\"table-wrap\\\"><table>\\n <thead><tr><th>Risk</th><th>Guardrail</th></tr></thead>\\n
      <tbody>\\n <tr><td>Accidental lifecycle interruption</td><td>Use distinct Start, Stop, and
      Restart buttons. Disable conflicting actions while busy. Confirm Stop/Restart and require
      stronger confirmation for global operations.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Host-only push</td><td>Show
      exact repository, path, branch, SHA, fast-forward mode, and commits. Preserve the CLI’s
      <code>PUSH</code> phrase; never auto-approve or hide force-with-lease.</td></tr>\\n
      <tr><td>Credential leakage</td><td>Never log environment values, Keychain contents, token
      prompts, or raw command environments. Keep GitHub setup in a terminal until a secure native
      wizard is explicitly designed.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Quarantine bypass</td><td>Use
      <code>msw</code>, not direct <code>msb</code>, for mutations. Model quarantine separately from
      lifecycle state and do not offer a “clear quarantine” button.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Destructive
      Docker cleanup</td><td>Default to volume-preserving cleanup. Make <code>--volumes</code> a
      separate, red, explicitly confirmed option.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Cold backup
      surprises</td><td>Before execution, show destination, sensitive contents, affected workspaces,
      and that running VMs will be stopped and then restored to their prior running
      set.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Restore damage</td><td>Keep restore out of the popover. Require
      checksum validation, archive inspection, typed <code>RESTORE</code>, and a final explanation
      that VMs remain stopped and Keychain tokens are not changed.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Untrusted
      arbitrary execution</td><td>Terminal-first for <code>exec</code>. If a native form is later
      added, pass validated argv and never interpolate a user string into a shell
      command.</td></tr>\\n <tr><td>Accessibility and localization</td><td>Use native
      Label/Button/Menu/Picker/TextField/SecureField/Toggle/ProgressView controls, visible text
      beside icons, VoiceOver labels that include workspace and state, keyboard focus order,
      semantic status text, and locale-aware FormatStyle APIs. Put strings in
      Localizable.xcstrings.</td></tr>\\n </tbody>\\n </table></div>\\n\\n <h2>7. Delivery
      phases</h2>\\n <div class=\\\"step\\\"><div class=\\\"step-num\\\">0</div><div><h3>Stabilize
      the machine interface</h3><p>Add and test versioned JSON modes for status, metrics, GitHub
      status, repositories, and ports. Add fixture-based parser tests and preserve current human
      output. This is the prerequisite that prevents a brittle Swift text parser.</p></div></div>\\n
      <div class=\\\"step\\\"><div class=\\\"step-num\\\">1</div><div><h3>Ship the monitor
      core</h3><p>Create <code>macos/MSWMonitor</code> as a macOS 14+ Xcode app. Implement the
      status item, three cards, status/metrics polling, Start/Stop/Restart, Refresh, settings, login
      item toggle, errors, stale data, Activity, and terminal fallback.</p></div></div>\\n <div
      class=\\\"step\\\"><div class=\\\"step-num\\\">2</div><div><h3>Ship daily workflow
      launchers</h3><p>Add Open site, Copy URL, Open in Zed, Ghostty shell handoff, ports picker,
      streaming logs, repository picker, clone, pull, and GitHub status/verify. Add the detail
      window and bounded operation history.</p></div></div>\\n <div class=\\\"step\\\"><div
      class=\\\"step-num\\\">3</div><div><h3>Ship guarded maintenance</h3><p>Add disk inspection,
      resize, backup, tunnel tracking, deep check, push review, and identity settings. Keep
      operations visible with progress and failure recovery.</p></div></div>\\n <div
      class=\\\"step\\\"><div class=\\\"step-num\\\">4</div><div><h3>Ship recovery and expert
      controls</h3><p>Add secure native flows only where they improve safety: clean, upgrade,
      update, host repair, GitHub setup/remove, restore, and optional canned exec actions. Terminal
      handoff remains a supported escape hatch.</p></div></div>\\n\\n <h2>8. Verification
      plan</h2>\\n <div class=\\\"grid\\\">\\n <section class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Pure Swift
      tests</h3><ul><li>JSON decoding and schema-version rejection.</li><li>Lifecycle
      transition/state-machine invariants.</li><li>Stale/partial data aggregation and status-item
      severity.</li><li>Argument construction and path validation.</li><li>Redaction and bounded
      output buffers.</li><li>Confirmation policy for every dangerous
      command.</li></ul></section>\\n <section class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Process integration
      tests</h3><ul><li>Fake <code>msw</code>/<code>msb</code> executables with controlled stdout,
      stderr, exit codes, delays, and streamed JSON Lines.</li><li>Cancellation terminates child
      processes without launching duplicate operations.</li><li>Missing CLI/config, missing Keychain
      access, quarantine, and stale data all render recoverable states.</li></ul></section>\\n
      <section class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Real Mac smoke test</h3><ul><li>Launch with all VMs stopped;
      verify no automatic starts.</li><li>Start <code>dev</code>, observe readiness and metrics,
      open a published site, open Zed and Ghostty, then stop.</li><li>Stream logs, run quick check,
      verify GitHub status, and exercise a failed command.</li><li>Test light/dark mode, VoiceOver,
      keyboard focus, notification opt-in, login item, signed build, and
      relaunch.</li></ul></section>\\n </div>\\n <div class=\\\"callout danger\\\"><strong>Do not
      use production backup/restore, credential rotation, force push, or destructive Docker cleanup
      as casual smoke tests.</strong> Cover their command planning and confirmation behavior with
      fakes; use a disposable workspace for real end-to-end validation.</div>\\n\\n <h2>9. Decisions
      to keep fixed unless a concrete need appears</h2>\\n <ul>\\n <li>macOS 14+ deployment target;
      SwiftUI <code>MenuBarExtra</code> with window style.</li>\\n <li>One calm icon; no status text
      or workspace names in the menu bar.</li>\\n <li>No automatic VM starts from
      monitoring.</li>\\n <li><code>msw</code> remains the policy boundary for mutations.</li>\\n
      <li>No App Sandbox for the first personal Developer ID build.</li>\\n <li>No global hotkey,
      arbitrary command form, or token wizard in the first release.</li>\\n <li>Settings persist
      only non-sensitive preferences: paths, favorites, polling, notifications, launch-at-login, and
      display choices.</li>\\n </ul>\\n\\n <h2>Sources and evidence</h2>\\n <details
      open><summary>Repository and runtime sources read</summary><ul><li><code>README.md</code> —
      workspace purposes, defaults, daily use, trust
      boundary.</li><li><code>docs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md</code> — complete command catalog and
      examples.</li><li><code>docs/SETUP-GUIDE.md</code> — lifecycle, ports, Git, backup, recovery,
      maintenance.</li><li><code>docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md</code> — Keychain split, read-only guest
      token, host-only push, verification, quarantine
      implications.</li><li><code>docs/TEST-REPORT.md</code> — 46 release scenarios and security
      invariants.</li><li><code>bin/msw</code>, <code>config.sh</code>, <code>setup.sh</code> —
      actual dispatch, side effects, environment, resources, and safety guards.</li><li>Installed
      <code>msb --help</code> and <code>msb --tree</code>; live read-only <code>msb status --all
      --format json</code> and <code>msb metrics --all --format json</code>
      output.</li></ul></details>\\n <details><summary>Apple platform references</summary><ul><li><a
      href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/menubarextra\\\">SwiftUI
      MenuBarExtra</a> and <a
      href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/scene/menubarextrastyle(_:)\\\">Men
      uBarExtra window style</a>.</li><li><a
      href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/servicemanagement/smappservice\\\">ServiceM
      anagement SMAppService</a> for launch-at-login.</li><li><a
      href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit/nsworkspace/openconfiguration\\\">NS
      Workspace.OpenConfiguration</a> for argv-based app handoff.</li><li><a
      href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit/nsstatusitem\\\">NSStatusItem</a>
      and <a href=\\\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit/nspopover\\\">NSPopover</a>
      as the deliberate AppKit fallback if native MenuBarExtra control proves
      insufficient.</li></ul></details>\\n <details><summary>Research panel</summary><p>Seven
      independent <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> research runs reviewed command inventory, SwiftUI/AppKit
      architecture, menu-bar UX, accessibility, safety, integration feasibility, and product
      prioritization. They made no repository code changes. Their convergent recommendations are
      reflected above: use <code>msw</code> for policy-bearing mutations, machine JSON for
      telemetry, progressive disclosure, explicit confirmations, stale-data semantics, and terminal
      fallback for sensitive workflows.</p></details>\\n\\n### quarantine\\nassert_not_quarantined()
      {\\n local box=\\\"$1\\\" file\\n [[ \\\"${MSW_ALLOW_QUARANTINED:-0}\\\" == 1 ]] && return
      0\\n file=\\\"$(quarantine_file \\\"$box\\\")\\\"\\n [[ ! -e \\\"$file\\\" && ! -L
      \\\"$file\\\" ]] || fatal \\\"workspace '$box' is quarantined; repair it with: msw github
      setup $box OWNER/REPO\\\"\\n}\\n\\nsandbox_running() {\\n local box=\\\"$1\\\" status\\n
      status=\\\"$(\\\"$MSB_BIN\\\" status \\\"$box\\\" --format json 2>/dev/null)\\\" || return
      2\\n status=\\\"$(printf '%s' \\\"$status\\\" | tr -d '[:space:]')\\\"\\n case \\\"$status\\\"
      in\\n *'\\\"status\\\":\\\"Running\\\"'*) return 0 ;;\\n *'\\\"status\\\":\\\"Stopped\\\"'*)
      return 1 ;;\\n *) return 2 ;;\\n esac\\n}\\n\\nquarantine_workspace() {\\n local
      box=\\\"$1\\\" reason=\\\"${2:-GitHub credential cleanup failed}\\\" file attempt=0
      stop_failed=0 running_rc inspect_rc\\n file=\\\"$(quarantine_file \\\"$box\\\")\\\"\\n mkdir
      -p \\\"$GITHUB_META_DIR\\\" || return 1\\n chmod 700 \\\"$GITHUB_META_DIR\\\" || return 1\\n
      umask 077 || return 1\\n printf '%s\\\\n' \\\"$reason\\\" >\\\"$file\\\" || return 1\\n if
